#: markdown/analysis.md:1
msgid ""
"For your benefit the [repository](https://github.com/blake-"
"armstrong/binding-tutorial-PLUMED/) contains a directory called "
"`reference_data` which contains all of the outputs that are produced from "
"the [running your simulations](inputs.md) section. If for some reason you "
"can't or don't want to run the simulations yourself, you can use the raw "
"data provided for analysis, or look at the analysis that is also included."
msgstr ""
"[リポジトリ](https://github.com/blake-armstrong/binding-tutorial-PLUMED/) の "
"`reference_data` には [実行](inputs.md) "
"の全出力があります。自分で実行できない、またはしない場合も、元データで解析したり、付属の解析結果を見たりできます。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:3
msgid "Installations"
msgstr "インストール"

#: markdown/analysis.md:5
msgid ""
"Before proceeding with the analysis, the script `mtd_analysis.py` requires a"
" couple of Python packages to be installed. Run the following command to "
"install them into your conda environment:"
msgstr "解析の `mtd_analysis.py` に必要な Python Package を、次で conda 環境に入れます。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:11
msgid "Analysis"
msgstr "解析"

#: markdown/analysis.md:14
msgid ""
"Once your simulations have finished the BIAS directory will contain all of "
"your HILLS files. If you see any `bck.HILLS.x` it is because there were "
"already HILLS files in the BIAS directory when the simulation began, and "
"were moved to backup before beginning to prevent overwriting them."
msgstr ""
"終了後、BIAS に HILLS が揃います。`bck.HILLS.x` は実行前に既存 HILLS があり、上書き防止のため Backup "
"に移されたものです。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:16
msgid ""
"In each `data/radius_0.x` directory you will find an 'analysis.sh' file. "
"Running the command `bash analysis.sh` will do the following:"
msgstr "各 `data/radius_0.x` の analysis.sh を `bash analysis.sh` で実行すると、次を行います。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:23
msgid ""
"This section will grab the value of $k_BT$ at 300 K using the PLUMED command"
" line tool. This value is required when producing the PMF."
msgstr "PLUMED コマンドラインで300 K の $k_BT$ を求めます。PMF に必要です。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:28
msgid ""
"Here all of the `HILLS.x` files in the `BIAS` directory will be concatenated"
" together to produce one main HILLS file."
msgstr "`BIAS` の全 `HILLS.x` を1つに連結します。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:33
msgid ""
"Here we use the `sum_hills` tool to process the combined HILLS file and "
"produce the one dimensional PMF. We manually pass in the value of kt and "
"tell PLUMED to translate the profile such that the minimum becomes zero."
msgstr "`sum_hills` で連結 HILLS から1次元 PMF を作ります。kt を手動で渡し、最小を0に揃えます。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:38
msgid ""
"This Python script will perform the analysis described in the [theory "
"section](theory.md), taking the file containing the 1D PMF, the spring "
"constant and radius for the flat-bottom cylindrical restraint, and the "
"temperature as input. To demonstrate this for the case of radius_0.0, once "
"completed it will print the following to the screen (and written to the file"
" `dG.dat`):"
msgstr ""
"[理論編](theory.md) の Python 解析は、1次元 PMF、Flat-bottom 円柱の Spring "
"Constant・半径、温度を入力に取ります。radius_0.0 では次が画面と `dG.dat` に出ます。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:72
msgid ""
"The first section, \"Binding Energy\", has computed the binding free energy "
"$\\Delta G_{PMF}$ as 23.08 kJ/mol using a set of hard-coded boundaries "
"(which can be modified if desired). The volume correction free energy "
"$\\Delta G_V$ for the unbound region is computed to be -18.06 kJ/mol from an"
" unbound volume of 0.0006497226 nm^3. Combining these two give a total "
"correction of 5.02 kJ/mol. This script also writes out the PMF with the "
"unbound region aligned to zero (`aligned_fes.dat`), making comparison with "
"other radii easier."
msgstr ""
"「Binding Energy」では、固定の境界（変更可能）で $\\Delta G_{PMF}$ = 23.08 kJ/mol "
"を計算します。非結合体積0.0006497226 nm^3から $\\Delta G_V$ = -18.06 kJ/mol を得て、合計は5.02 "
"kJ/mol です。非結合領域を0に揃えた `aligned_fes.dat` も出力し、半径間で比較しやすくします。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:74
msgid ""
"The final correction for the bound volume explored $\\Delta G_R$ is usually "
"performed with alchemical free energy perturbation, however, in this simple "
"system we make an analytical estimate, which is presented as 4.62 kJ/mol in "
"the \"Bound Correction\" section of the output. Briefly, the analytical "
"estimate works by fitting a harmonic potential to the minimum produced by "
"the Gaussian and using that to compute an estimate of the unrestrained bound"
" volume using the equation for the volume of a 3D harmonic oscillator in the"
" [theory section](theory.md). This fit is written to `fit_harmonic.dat`. The"
" volume of the restrained bound volume is then estimated using the equations"
" for the area of a 2D harmonic oscillator (for the area in the xy plane) and"
" the length for a 1D harmonic oscillator (to estimate the height of the "
"restrained cylinder along z using the fit). The ratio of these two produce a"
" free energy correction very similar to that produced by alchemical methods."
" In the case of radii greater than zero, the restrained bound volume is "
"greater than the unrestrained bound volume, resulting in a free energy "
"correction of 0 kJ/mol for the removal of the cylindrical restraint."
msgstr ""
"結合領域の体積補正 $\\Delta G_R$ は通常 Alchemical Free Energy Perturbation "
"で求めますが、この単純な系では解析的に推定し、「Bound Correction」に4.62 kJ/mol と表示します。Gaussian の極小を "
"Harmonic Potential に Fit し、[理論編](theory.md) の3次元 Harmonic Oscillator "
"の体積から非拘束体積を推定します。Fit は `fit_harmonic.dat` に保存します。拘束体積は、xy の2次元 Oscillator "
"の面積と、Fit による z の1次元 Oscillator の長さから推定します。両体積比の自由エネルギー補正は Alchemical "
"法とよく一致します。半径が0超では拘束体積が非拘束体積より大きいため、円柱除去の補正は0 kJ/mol です。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:76
msgid ""
"Combing $\\Delta G_{PMF}$, $\\Delta G_V$ and $\\Delta G_R$ produces a final "
"standard binding free energy of 9.65 kJ/mol. This value should be the same "
"for every radius (to within $k_BT$), given the entire unbound volume is "
"sampled completely."
msgstr ""
"$\\Delta G_{PMF}$、$\\Delta G_V$、$\\Delta G_R$ を合わせ、標準結合自由エネルギー9.65 kJ/mol "
"を得ます。非結合体積全体を十分 Sampling すれば、全半径で $k_BT$ 以内で一致するはずです。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:78
msgid ""
"Included below is a table of the standard binding free energies as a "
"function of the radius of the flat-bottom cylindrical harmonic restraint."
msgstr "半径に対する標準結合自由エネルギーを表に示します。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:80
msgid "Radius (nm)"
msgstr "半径 (nm)"

#: markdown/analysis.md:80
msgid "$\\Delta G_{PMF}$ (kJ/mol)"
msgstr "$\\Delta G_{PMF}$ (kJ/mol)"

#: markdown/analysis.md:80
msgid "$\\Delta G_{V}$ (kJ/mol)"
msgstr "$\\Delta G_{V}$ (kJ/mol)"

#: markdown/analysis.md:80
msgid "$\\Delta G_{R}$ (kJ/mol)"
msgstr "$\\Delta G_{R}$ (kJ/mol)"

#: markdown/analysis.md:80
msgid "$\\Delta G^{⦵}$ (kJ/mol)"
msgstr "$\\Delta G^{⦵}$ (kJ/mol)"

#: markdown/analysis.md:90
msgid ""
"Qualitatively, one can see the agreement to within $k_BT$. A keen student "
"might feel inclined to run replicates and perform a statistical analysis to "
"quantitatively show that they are in agreement, but that is left as further "
"work and not performed here."
msgstr "定性的には $k_BT$ 以内の一致がわかります。独立実行と統計解析で定量的に確かめてもよいですが、ここでは今後の課題とします。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:92
msgid ""
"A simple gnuplot script for visualising the PMFs of the different radii all "
"together has been provided as `scripts/fes.gnuplot`. Once the simulations "
"have all run the data can be visualised as follow:"
msgstr "異なる半径の PMF をまとめる `scripts/fes.gnuplot` を用意しています。全実行後、次で可視化できます。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:103
msgid ""
"One-dimensional PMFs (aligned to the unbound region) as a function of the "
"radius of the flat-bottom cylindrical restraining potential, and how they "
"compared to the input potential energy surface (shown with the dashed red "
"line). This representation highlights how the relative stability of the "
"bound region to the unbound region decreases with increasing radius. The "
"dissolution barrier decreases with increasing radius, as the ligand can more"
" freely move around the barrier in the x and y directions."
msgstr ""
"Flat-bottom 円柱の半径ごとの、非結合領域を0にした1次元 PMF と、入力 Potential Energy "
"Surface（赤破線）の比較です。半径が増すと、非結合状態に対する結合領域の相対安定性が低下します。Ligand が x・y 方向に Barrier "
"を回避しやすくなるため、Dissolution Barrier も下がります。"

#: markdown/analysis.md:106
msgid ""
"This figure makes apparent how the height of the free energy barrier is "
"dependent on the radius of the cylinder, and why it is important to be able "
"to use large flat-bottom cylinders when performing actual binding "
"simulations when the barriers are of interest."
msgstr ""
"この図は Barrier 高さの半径依存性と、実際の結合で Barrier を知りたい場合に大きな Flat-bottom 円柱が重要な理由を示します。"

